    "title": "NHL Roundup: Senators Beat Rangers, Devils Win in OT, Sabres Defeat Flyers",
    "text": "• The Ottawa Senators defeated the New York Rangers 8-4 on Wednesday night.\n• Brady Tkachuk scored his 200th regular-season NHL goal and had three assists.\n• The Rangers have lost five consecutive games.\n• The Senators scored four goals in the first period at Madison Square Garden.\n• The Rangers are in last place in the Eastern Conference.\n• Jonathan Quick allowed six goals on 17 shots for the Rangers.\n• Leevi Merilainen made 18 saves for the Senators.\n• The New Jersey Devils defeated the Seattle Kraken 3-2 in overtime.\n• Nico Hischier scored the game-winning goal for the Devils.\n• The Buffalo Sabres defeated the Philadelphia Flyers 5-2.\n• Rasmus Dahlin scored two power-play goals for the Sabres.\n• The Sabres have won 14 of their last 16 games.\n• The Flyers have lost four games in a row.",
